values
  ('fe-g00001', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-botany', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the scientific name of the Narra tree, which is commonly found in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Pterocarpus indicus"},{"id":"b","text":"Ficus elastica"},{"id":"c","text":"Acacia mangium"},{"id":"d","text":"Swietenia mahagoni"}]'::jsonb, 'a',
   'The scientific name of the Narra tree, which is commonly found in the Philippines, is Pterocarpus indicus. This species is well-known for its durable wood and is often used in furniture making and construction.',
   'Pterocarpus indicus is the correct scientific name for the Narra tree, a species native to Southeast Asia, including the Philippines. Ficus elastica refers to the rubber tree, Acacia mangium is a fast-growing tree used for reforestation, and Swietenia mahagoni is the scientific name for mahogany, which is not native to the Philippines. The Narra tree is significant in Philippine culture and is even considered the national tree of the Philippines.',
   'Remember that Narra is the national tree of the Philippines, and its scientific name is Pterocarpus indicus.',
   now(), 'gpt-4o'),
  ('fe-g00002', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-botany', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which family does the Philippine Mahogany, also known as Lauan, belong to?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Fabaceae"},{"id":"b","text":"Myrtaceae"},{"id":"c","text":"Dipterocarpaceae"},{"id":"d","text":"Moraceae"}]'::jsonb, 'c',
   'The Philippine Mahogany, also known as Lauan, belongs to the Dipterocarpaceae family. This family is known for its large hardwood trees that are prevalent in Southeast Asian forests.',
   'The correct family for Philippine Mahogany or Lauan is Dipterocarpaceae. This family includes many important timber trees in the Philippines. Fabaceae is the legume family, which includes peas and beans. Myrtaceae is a family that includes eucalyptus and guava, and Moraceae includes figs and mulberries. Dipterocarpaceae is the dominant family in lowland rainforests of the Philippines, making it the correct choice.',
   'Associate Lauan with Dipterocarpaceae, the dominant tree family in Philippine rainforests.',
   now(), 'gpt-4o'),
  ('fe-g00003', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-botany', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the common name of the tree with the scientific name Dipterocarpus gracilis, commonly found in Philippine forests?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Yakal"},{"id":"b","text":"Bagras"},{"id":"c","text":"Banaba"},{"id":"d","text":"Apitong"}]'::jsonb, 'd',
   'The common name of the tree with the scientific name Dipterocarpus gracilis is Apitong. This species is commonly found in Philippine forests and is valued for its timber.',
   'Dipterocarpus gracilis is known as Apitong in the Philippines. Yakal is another type of hardwood tree, Bagras refers to Eucalyptus deglupta, and Banaba is Lagerstroemia speciosa, known for its medicinal properties. Apitong is a significant timber species in the Philippines, often used in construction and furniture making.',
   'Link Dipterocarpus species with Apitong, a common timber tree in the Philippines.',
   now(), 'gpt-4o'),
  ('fe-g00004', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-botany', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the scientific name of the Benguet Pine, a species native to the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Pinus sylvestris"},{"id":"b","text":"Pinus kesiya"},{"id":"c","text":"Pinus insularis"},{"id":"d","text":"Pinus merkusii"}]'::jsonb, 'c',
   'The scientific name of the Benguet Pine, a species native to the Philippines, is Pinus insularis. This species is adapted to the highland areas of Luzon.',
   'Pinus insularis is the correct scientific name for the Benguet Pine, which is native to the highlands of Luzon in the Philippines. Pinus sylvestris is the Scots Pine, native to Europe and Asia. Pinus kesiya is the Khasi Pine, found in South Asia, and Pinus merkusii is the Merkus Pine, native to Southeast Asia but not specifically the Philippines. The Benguet Pine is adapted to the cooler climates of the Philippine highlands, making Pinus insularis the correct choice.',
   'Remember that Benguet Pine is native to the Philippines and is scientifically named Pinus insularis.',
   now(), 'gpt-4o'),
  ('fe-g00005', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-botany', 'Medium', 'practice',
