   '[{"id":"a","text":"Verbenaceae"},{"id":"b","text":"Dipterocarpaceae"},{"id":"c","text":"Lamiaceae"},{"id":"d","text":"Fabaceae"}]'::jsonb, 'a',
   'The family name of Tectona philippinensis, the Philippine teak tree, is Verbenaceae. This family is known for including trees and shrubs with opposite leaves and often aromatic properties.',
   'Tectona philippinensis belongs to the Verbenaceae family, which is characterized by its woody plants, often with aromatic leaves. The other options are incorrect: Dipterocarpaceae is a family known for large tropical trees like Dipterocarps; Lamiaceae is primarily known for herbs and shrubs like mint and basil; Fabaceae is the legume family, which includes beans and peas.',
   'Remember that Tectona species, like teak, are in the Verbenaceae family.',
   now(), 'gpt-4o'),
  ('fe-g00006', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-botany', 'Medium', 'practice',
