   'Swietenia macrophylla is commonly known as Mahogany. It is a large tropical tree valued for its high-quality timber.',
   'Swietenia macrophylla is Mahogany, a tree species highly prized for its durable and attractive wood. Molave (Vitex parviflora) is a different species known for its hard wood; Bamboo is a grass, not a tree; Mangrove refers to various species adapted to coastal environments, not specifically Swietenia macrophylla.',
