   'Hopea foxworthyi is commonly known as Yakal Saplungan. It is a species found in Philippine dipterocarp forests, known for its hard and durable wood.',
   'Hopea foxworthyi, or Yakal Saplungan, is a member of the Dipterocarpaceae family, recognized for its strong and heavy wood. Manggachapui (Hopea acuminata) and White Lauan (Shorea contorta) are different species within the same family, and Narra (Pterocarpus indicus) belongs to the Fabaceae family.',
