   'Ficus balete is commonly known as the Balete Tree. It is a type of fig tree often found in Philippine lowland forests.',
   'Ficus balete, or the Balete Tree, is a species of fig known for its aerial roots and cultural significance in the Philippines. The Banyan Tree is a different species of fig, Toog Tree (Petersianthus quadrialatus) is unrelated, and Narra Tree (Pterocarpus indicus) belongs to the Fabaceae family.',
