   '[{"id":"a","text":"Fabaceae"},{"id":"b","text":"Meliaceae"},{"id":"c","text":"Anacardiaceae"},{"id":"d","text":"Dipterocarpaceae"}]'::jsonb, 'd',
   'Shorea contorta, known as Lauan, is part of the Dipterocarpaceae family. This family is characterized by its large trees and valuable timber, commonly found in mixed species plantations in the Philippines.',
   'Option c is correct because Shorea contorta is a member of the Dipterocarpaceae family. Option a, Fabaceae, includes legumes and is unrelated to Shorea. Option b, Meliaceae, includes Mahogany but not Shorea. Option d, Anacardiaceae, includes cashews and mangoes, which are not related to Shorea.',
   'Lauan species belong to the Dipterocarpaceae family, known for their timber value.',
