   '[{"id":"a","text":"To provide legal land tenure to upland farmers and promote sustainable land use."},{"id":"b","text":"To increase timber exports by allowing private corporations to manage forest lands."},{"id":"c","text":"To establish protected areas and restrict all forms of human activity within them."},{"id":"d","text":"To privatize all government-owned forest lands to increase revenue."}]'::jsonb, 'a',
   'The Forest Occupancy Management Program aimed to provide legal land tenure to upland farmers, ensuring they had the right to use the land sustainably. This was part of a broader effort to promote sustainable land use and improve the livelihoods of upland communities.',
   'Option a is correct because the Forest Occupancy Management Program was designed to address issues of land tenure insecurity among upland farmers, encouraging them to adopt sustainable practices by providing them legal rights to the land. Option b is incorrect because the program was not focused on increasing timber exports or involving private corporations in forest management. Option c is incorrect as the program did not aim to establish protected areas with restrictions on human activity; rather, it sought to integrate human activity with sustainable land management. Option d is incorrect because the program did not involve privatization of forest lands; it was about providing tenure to existing occupants.',
