   'During the American colonial period, a centralized government body was established to manage forest resources and enforce conservation laws, which was crucial in organizing and regulating forest use.',
   'Option d is correct because the establishment of a centralized government body, such as the Bureau of Forestry, was a key strategy during the American colonial period to manage forests and prevent illegal logging. Option a is incorrect because while forestry education was important, the primary strategy was centralized management. Option b is incorrect as a nationwide logging ban was not implemented; instead, regulation and management were emphasized. Option c is incorrect because promoting free-license logging would counteract efforts to control and manage forest use.',
