   'Executive Order No. 263 in 1995 was significant because it marked the formal adoption of Community-Based Forest Management (CBFM) as the national strategy for sustainable forestry in the Philippines. This approach emphasizes the involvement of local communities in managing forest resources, aiming to balance ecological sustainability with economic benefits for the communities.',
   'Option a is correct because Executive Order No. 263 explicitly established Community-Based Forest Management as the national strategy, promoting the involvement of local communities in forest management to ensure sustainability and equitable resource sharing. Option b is incorrect as it refers to Industrial Forest Management Agreements, which are separate initiatives aimed at private sector involvement. Option c is incorrect because the Forest Products Research and Development Institute was established earlier, in 1954, not by this executive order. Option d is incorrect as the National Greening Program was launched much later, in 2011, under a different initiative.',
   'Remember that Executive Order No. 263 is associated with community involvement in forestry.',
   now(), 'gpt-4o'),
