   'During the American Colonial Period, the establishment of forest reserves in the Philippines was primarily focused on preserving watersheds. This was driven by the need to protect water supplies essential for agricultural and municipal purposes, reflecting the American emphasis on resource management and conservation.',
   'Option b is correct because during the American Colonial Period, the focus was on watershed protection to secure water supply for agriculture and municipal use, aligning with American conservation policies. Option a is incorrect as the Spanish Colonial Era did not prioritize watershed preservation for defense. Option c is incorrect because post-World War II efforts were more about reforestation and rehabilitation rather than watershed preservation. Option d is incorrect as the Martial Law Period focused on political control rather than environmental conservation.',
