   'The Integrated Social Forestry Program, introduced in 1982, aimed to promote sustainable livelihoods for upland communities by integrating land tenure and resource management. This program addressed issues related to forest land use by providing secure land tenure to local communities, encouraging sustainable forest management practices.',
   'Option c is correct because the Integrated Social Forestry Program focused on improving the livelihoods of upland communities through secure land tenure and sustainable resource management. Option a is incorrect as the program did not prioritize industrial logging; instead, it aimed at community-based management. Option b is incorrect because the program did not primarily focus on decentralizing forest management to local governments. Option d is incorrect as the program was not about establishing large-scale plantations for timber exports.',
