   'The Indigenous Peoples'' Rights Act (RA 8371) aims to recognize and promote the rights of indigenous cultural communities, particularly their rights to ancestral domains, which include forest lands. This law is crucial for ensuring that indigenous peoples can manage and protect their traditional lands.',
