   '[{"id":"a","text":"Ensure the sustainable management and utilization of forest resources."},{"id":"b","text":"Oversee the enforcement of national logging bans."},{"id":"c","text":"Set national forest policy and legislative priorities."},{"id":"d","text":"Classify public lands into forest land or alienable and disposable land."}]'::jsonb, 'a',
   'The primary responsibility of the People''s Organization (PO) under the Community-Based Forest Management Agreement (CBFMA) is to ensure the sustainable management and utilization of forest resources. This aligns with the objectives of the CBFMS, which aims to empower local communities to manage forest resources sustainably.',
   'Option b is correct because the CBFMS is designed to involve local communities in the sustainable management and utilization of forest resources. This responsibility is crucial for achieving the goals of environmental conservation and community development. Option a is incorrect because overseeing national logging bans is a function typically handled by government agencies, not POs. Option c is incorrect as setting national forest policy and legislative priorities is a role for national government bodies, not local organizations. Option d is incorrect because classifying public lands is a technical and legal process managed by government agencies, not POs.',
   'Remember that in community-based strategies, local organizations focus on sustainable management and utilization of resources.',
