   'Under PD 705, a Special Land Use Permit (SLUP) is required for activities that involve the establishment of structures within forest lands. Recreational structures fall under this category as they alter the landscape and require specific management to ensure minimal environmental impact.',
   'Option b is correct because the establishment of any structure for recreational purposes within forest lands requires a Special Land Use Permit (SLUP) as per PD 705. This is to ensure that such developments do not harm the forest ecosystem. Option a is incorrect because road construction for forest management is typically covered under different permits related to forest management activities. Option c is incorrect as indigenous communities have specific rights to collect non-timber forest products under certain conditions without needing a SLUP. Option d is incorrect because scientific research activities are generally covered by separate research permits rather than a SLUP.',
